      "text": "To find the area of the square, we first need to determine the length of one of its sides. According to the problem, the edge of the square can be expressed in two different ways: \\(4x - 15\\) meters or \\(20 - 3x\\) meters. Since both expressions represent the same edge length, we can set them equal to each other and solve for \\(x\\).\n\n\\[\n4x - 15 = 20 - 3x\n\\]\n\nFirst, we will add \\(3x\\) to both sides of the equation to combine the \\(x\\) terms on one side:\n\n\\[\n4x + 3x - 15 = 20 - 3x + 3x\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n7x - 15 = 20\n\\]\n\nNext, we add 15 to both sides to isolate the term with \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\n7x - 15 + 15 = 20 + 15\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n7x = 35\n\\]\n\nNow, we divide both sides by 7 to solve for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{35}{7} = 5\n\\]\n\nNow that we have the value of \\(x\\), we can substitute it back into either expression for the side length of the square to find the actual length of the side. Let's use \\(4x - 15\\):\n\n\\[\n4(5) - 15 = 20 - 15 = 5 \\text{ meters}\n\\]\n\nSo, the side length of the square is 5 meters. The area of a square is given by the square of its side length. Therefore, the area is:\n\n\\[\n5^2 = 25 \\text{ square meters}\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of the square is \\(\\boxed{25}\\).",
